# macOS: the Objective-C classes of the multimedia, positioning, gamepad and
# speech plugins on the 32-bit runtime (the i386 port).
#
# The 32-bit (fragile) Objective-C runtime fixes each instance variable's
# offset when the class is compiled, from its @interface, and so accepts
# instance variables only there - not in the @implementation, not in a class
# extension - and synthesizes no property by itself. Qt 5.15 was written for
# the 64-bit runtime only.
#
# The AVFoundation camera and player observers, the asset writer, the display
# link observer, the CoreLocation delegate, the gamepad manager and the speech
# state delegate declare their variables in the @interface; the gamepad
# manager's two observer properties get variables and @synthesize. On i386
# the gamepad backend does not start: GameController has no 32-bit slice,
# and the i386 build does not link it.
#
# Nothing else changes in behaviour, on any architecture.
#
# Apply: git apply, from the Qt source root
